# scan-public allowlist for hollis-labs/tether (tree findings only).
# Format: RULE-ID PATH-GLOB REASON. One line per file and rule, no pattern entries. Entries
# cover the whole file, not a line, so a new finding in a listed file is allowlisted too; the
# scanner still prints every allowlisted finding and reports them as not counted, so nothing is
# hidden. Each reason says what the left side is and why the value stays. History findings are
# not covered here.
secret-assignment cmd/tether-apikey-helper/main_test.go Two local consts named secret hold the plaintext value the keyring decoder must return unchanged; each is a descriptive fake used within its own subtest.
secret-assignment cmd/tether/credentials_test.go Left side is the TETHER_TOKEN environment variable handed to the code under test; the value is a canary the test asserts does not survive into the generated MCP config (the token must come out empty).
secret-assignment cmd/tether/doctor_credentials_test.go Local const named secret is a canary the doctor output must never contain; the check only means something if the canary is distinctive.
secret-assignment docs/secrets.md Documentation example of the file:// credential-reference syntax; the value is the path of a token file, not a credential.
secret-assignment e2e/a2a_wiring_test.go Left side is the bearer_token field of the A2A peer config read by the code under test; the value is the fake token the e2e peer must present and is checked again in the file.
secret-assignment internal/a2aadapter/adapter_test.go Left sides are the adapter BearerToken config field; the values are fake credentials the test presents or withholds to see a request accepted or refused.
secret-assignment internal/app/codex_auth_test.go Fixture auth file in the shape the Codex CLI writes, so OPENAI_API_KEY is its field name; the value says in words that it is not a real key.
secret-assignment internal/app/codex_review2_test.go Left side is the GH_TOKEN environment variable set in a catalog launch plan; the test asserts catalog environment is not recorded as the caller environment and never inspects the value.
secret-assignment internal/app/protected_paths_test.go Codex -c override text (model_provider.api_key) used as input to the helper that names an unrecognised argument for logging; the setting name is Codex own and the test asserts the returned name does not contain the value prefix.
secret-assignment internal/app/routing_reply_review_test.go Local const named secret is the reply text; the test asserts that no recorded event carries it.
secret-assignment internal/app/session_identity_test.go Left side is the TETHER_TOKEN environment variable of a parent session; the value is a marker the test compares again.
secret-assignment internal/app/session_mcp_policy_test.go Left sides are the TETHER_TOKEN and UPSTREAM_SECRET environment variables placed in a launch plan; the values are markers the test looks for in the stored policy.
secret-assignment internal/broker/service_test.go A JSON payload body whose field is named secret; the test asserts the payload never appears in the recorded event. The field name is incidental and the value is a fake.
secret-assignment internal/config/mcp_credfile_test.go A local const holds the content written to a temporary credential file and read back through a file:// reference; the yaml keys token and TESSERACT_TOKEN are the MCP server fields whose file:// references the test pins.
secret-assignment internal/config/mcp_server_test.go Left sides are MCP server config fields and environment variables (HADRON_TOKEN, token, OPENAI_API_KEY), keychain and helper reference strings the loader resolves, and one local const; the reference syntax is what the test pins and the values recur in the assertions.
secret-assignment internal/credfile/credfile_test.go Local const named secret is the content of a temporary credential file that the loader must return exactly, including newline trimming.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/credfile_redaction_test.go The two consts at the top hold fake credentials written to temporary credential files that the redactor must scrub; the inline Token field and the in-memory const are fake values for other redaction cases, including a short-value case. The redactor needs distinct values of realistic length to be tested.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/daemon_upstream_env_test.go Left side is the UPSTREAM_TOKEN environment variable whose reaching the daemon upstream is tested; the value is a descriptive marker checked again in the file.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/extract_test.go JSON key token in an argument fixture whose value the reference extractor must ignore (it extracts only allowlisted reference shapes); the value is sequential characters, not a key.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/forwarded_context_test.go The serviceToken field of the forwarded-context transport under test; the value is a descriptive marker checked in the assertions.
credentials-in-url internal/mcpadapter/forwarded_context_test.go A URL with userinfo on a reserved example host, used to test that credentials inside an upstream URL are refused; the userinfo is a placeholder.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/middleware_logging_redact_test.go Local const named secret is a fake value that must not appear in the recorded event error text.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/naming_test.go The Token field of an MCP server entry whose redaction in probe output is tested; the value is a placeholder repeated in the assertions.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/provenance_test.go progressToken is an MCP protocol field name, not a credential.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/proxy_error_redaction_test.go Local consts named secret hold fake credentials the proxy error redaction must remove; one is three ordinary words and nine digits placed in the path of a local test server URL, because a secret embedded in a URL is the case under test.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/shared_gateway_view_test.go A grouped const declaration holding two canaries, a hidden origin name and a value named secret, neither of which may appear in the shared gateway view.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/shared_upstreams_test.go Left side is the CATALOG_FIXTURE_SECRET environment variable of a fixture upstream whose handling is under test; the value is a descriptive marker.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/telemetry_test.go A tool argument named password whose value telemetry must not retain; the test asserts the canary is absent from persisted events. The argument name is incidental.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/upstream_recovery_test.go The FIXTURE_TOKEN environment variable of a fixture upstream, and a local const named secret that must not appear in the stderr tail; both are descriptive markers.
secret-assignment internal/mcpadapter/upstream_stdio_identity_test.go Left sides are the TETHER_TOKEN, TETHER_MCP_TOKEN and TETHER_OTHER_TOKEN environment variables whose stripping from a stdio upstream identity is tested; the values are markers compared again in the file.
secret-assignment internal/mcpforward/forward_test.go progressToken is an MCP protocol field name, not a credential.
agent-box-host testdata/launch-specs/launches/agent-workspaces-claude-stream-worktree.yaml The work_dir contains the directory name of the operator workspace root, not a network host. The parity test diffs this spec against the live catalog and reports a work_dir difference on any host that has the launch, so it cannot change here without changing the live catalog first. Remove this entry when the catalog and corpus move together.
